<h1>set cover</h1>
<p>
(classic problem)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A <a href="set.html"><em>set</em></a> of sets whose <a href="union.html"><em>union</em></a> has all members of the union of all sets.  The set cover problem is to find a minimum size set.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Formal Definition:</strong> Given a set S of sets, choose c &sube; S such that  <strong>U</strong><sub>i=1</sub> c<sub>i</sub> = <strong>U</strong><sub>i=1</sub> S<sub>i</sub>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="covering.html"><em>covering</em></a>.
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
<a href="https://algorist.com/problems/Set_Cover.html" target="_blank">(Pascal)</a>

